ADDENDA <Act No. 34946, Oct. 18, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on October 20, 2024.
Article 2 (Timing of application of criminal justice procedures to investigative agencies, etc.)
The timing for the application of criminal justice procedures to investigative agencies, etc., in accordance with the proviso of Article 1 of the Addenda of the Act on the Use of Electronic Documents in Criminal Justice Procedures (Act No. 18485), shall be October 10, 2025.
Article 3 (Applicability to consolidated cases)
Where cases are consolidated during the investigation process, even if the investigation for a portion of the consolidated cases commenced before the timing of application prescribed in Article 2 of the Addenda, the entirety of such cases after consolidation shall be deemed cases for which the investigation commenced after the timing of application prescribed in Article 2 of the Addenda, and this Decree shall apply.
Article 4 (Special cases concerning cases subject to the former Act on the Use of Electronic Documents in Summary Proceedings)
(1) Where a summary order is requested via electronic document for a case subject to the former Act on the Use of Electronic Documents in Summary Proceedings after the enforcement of this Decree, the electronic processing of criminal justice procedures for such case by investigative agencies, etc., shall follow the examples of the former Act on the Use of Electronic Documents in Summary Proceedings until the timing of application prescribed in Article 2 of the Addenda.
(2) Procedures conducted in accordance with the examples of the former Act on the Use of Electronic Documents in Summary Proceedings before the timing of application prescribed in Article 2 of the Addenda under paragraph (1) shall be deemed procedures conducted in accordance with the Act and this Decree.
Article 5 (Special cases concerning investigation records and evidence records)
If an investigative agency, etc., receives a referral of a case from an entity other than an investigative agency, etc. in a form other than an electronic document and subsequently requests a warrant, etc., from a court, or institutes a prosecution or referral, the investigative records and evidence records of the relevant case need not be prepared or submitted as electronic documents until September 27, 2026.
Article 6 (Special cases concerning service and notification to persons under arrest, detention, confinement, or placement)
If electronic service or notification is to be made to a person who is arrested, under custody, or detained in a prison, detention center, or a holding cell of a national police station, notwithstanding Article 24(2), the service or notification shall be made by means of delivering a paper document printed from an electronic document until September 27, 2026.

